{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "expand-criteria-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7d, the POLLUTANT dimension: the `expand-criteria` RunSpec -- THC, CO and NOx running exhaust -- computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE. It mounts `moves-onroad.esm`, which carries the 54 default-database tables and the onroad model, and supplies the fourteen things that are this run's: thirteen runspec selections and the expected output, plus one binding. It is the seventh RunSpec this domain document reproduces and the first to leave the energy and particulate pollutants.\n\nIT WAS PENDING FOR A DAY, and what it waited on is worth keeping because it says what a RunSpec in this directory is for. With both rate tables read and the NOx humidity correction applied the entire gap was ONE multiplicative factor, `criteriaRatio`, measured at 8e-06 (PLAN.md §7.3.13); that table is EMPTY in the default database and MOVES computes all 4,398 of its rows at run time, TWO DIFFERENT WAYS, without recording which. The closed form landed 309 of the 372 cells and left 63 -- gasoline, model years 1980 to 2000, the EPA Complex Model's half to the row (§7.3.14). Both halves are now here.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES, which §23 asks for before a dimension is called covered.\n\n* THE RATE TABLE HAS TWO ARMS, AND EVERY EARLIER RUNSPEC USED ONLY ONE. `emissionRate` and `emissionRateByAge` are disjoint in pollutant-process: a pollutant either deteriorates with age or it does not. Tire wear, brake wear and running energy are in the first and every RunSpec in this directory until now read nothing else; THC, CO and NOx running exhaust are in the second, which has an `ageGroupID` key and 1,590,830 rows against the first's 105,449. Before J58 this run returned ZERO for all 375 cells. Conventions §67.1 has the selection that reads one arm or the other and why it is not a sum.\n\n* THE SHAPE COMES OUT OF THE RATE TABLE, TWICE. This run emits 124 cohorts where every other run of source type 21 emits 125, and 3 pollutant-process blocks where 4 pass the road-type test. The model year 2000 ELECTRICITY cohort has no `emissionRateByAge` row at its age group, so it is not rated and not emitted, while model years 2001-2020 of the same fuel are rated at ZERO and are; and SO2 running exhaust is selected, happens on a road, and has no rate row anywhere. Both were papered over while this document was pending -- the first by the `n_outputCohort` binding below, which was exact only because the unrated cohort happened to rank LAST -- and both are now RULES: a cohort or a pollutant-process with no rate is not emitted (conventions §67.2). Six RunSpecs could not tell that rule from `true` (§23).\n\n* THE SURVIVING POLLUTANT-PROCESSES ARE NOT A PREFIX. Eight are selected and three are emitted, at positions 1, 3 and 5. This is the one run in the corpus that would discriminate a renumbering of the output blocks (conventions §60).\n\n* THE NOx HUMIDITY ADJUSTMENT IS LIVE, ON BOTH OF ITS EQUATIONS. `noxhumidityadjust` carries CFR 86 -- linear in bounded specific humidity -- for gasoline and E85, and CFR 1065 -- reciprocal in bounded water mole fraction -- for diesel, and this run exercises both, at 1.0215928 and 1.0095484. No RunSpec here could see either before, because neither energy nor tire wear is NOx.\n\n* BOTH HALVES OF `criteriaRatio` ARE EXERCISED, AND NOTHING ELSE IN THE CORPUS EXERCISES EITHER. The closed form runs for gasoline model years 2001-2020, all of diesel and all of E85; the EPA Complex Model plus the sulfur model runs for gasoline 1980-2000. The factor ranges from 0.501 to 1.044 and NOx gasoline model years 2001-2016 is a factor of two, so it is not a correction -- it is half the answer. It also reaches the E85 property substitution (`FuelEffectsGenerator.setup()` step 020), which no snapshot-fed document can see at all, because every captured `fuelformulation` in the corpus already has it applied.\n\nTHE ONE BINDING. `n_outputCohort` is 124 and not the default 125, for the reason above. It is a DECLARATION that `cohortSurvivorCount` recomputes and run-tests.sh compares, so it is checked rather than asserted -- which is exactly what it was not while this document was pending.\n\nAGAINST `runspecs/process-tirewear.esm` it differs in its fourteen `url_template`s, in the one binding, and in nothing else: the same county, month, day, hour, source type and road type, and a different list of pollutant-processes. That is the point -- the dimension under test is the pollutant, and every other selection is held fixed.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "expand-criteria",
      "criteria-pollutants"
    ]
  },
